@startuml
title NitroCircus - Integrations and Trust Boundaries

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

rectangle "Trusted Core" {
  component "Telegram Bot" as BOT
  component "Orchestrator API" as API
  database "MongoDB" as DB
  queue "Redis" as REDIS
}

rectangle "Controlled Execution Boundary" {
  component "agent-runner" as RUNNER
  folder "isolated runner repo" as RR
}

cloud "GitHub API / Actions" as GH
cloud "Telegram Bot API" as TG
cloud "LLM Providers" as LLM
rectangle "NightCityVerse" as MV
cloud "External Integrations\n(e.g. WhatsApp, others)" as EXT

BOT --> TG : bot messages
BOT --> API : internal commands
API --> DB : state + audit
API --> REDIS : task queues
API --> GH : issues / board / bundle publish
API --> MV : visual events
REDIS --> RUNNER : queue consumption
RUNNER --> RR : code changes
RUNNER --> API : callback only
RUNNER --> GH : branches / PRs
RUNNER --> LLM : model execution
API --> EXT : optional/configurable integrations

note right of EXT
Regla operativa:
si falta configuración de terceros,
el sistema debe degradar o mockear,
no romper el arranque base.
end note

note bottom of RUNNER
No debe modificar producción directamente.
No debe usar el checkout productivo
como workspace.
end note

note left of GH
Fuente de verdad del trabajo visible:
issues, labels, project board, PRs,
bundles top-level publicados.
end note

note left of DB
Fuente de verdad operativa:
proyectos, tareas, transiciones,
event logs y agent runs.
end note

@enduml
